Build a Full Ubuntu Lab
Step 1: Create Project Folder
PowerShell:

mkdir -p ~/ubuntu-lab
cd ~/ubuntu-lab
UCRT64 / Git Bash:

mkdir -p ~/ubuntu-lab
cd ~/ubuntu-lab
Step 2: Create Dockerfile (No .txt!)
Run notepad Dockerfile and paste:
FROM ubuntu:22.04
ENV DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive
# Full Linux Admin toolkit - RHCSA / 31 LPA Roadmap ready
RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y \
    iproute2 net-tools iputils-ping dnsutils netcat-openbsd traceroute curl wget \
    procps htop systemd systemd-sysv psmisc lsof \
    vim nano sudo less man-db tree file rsync zip unzip \
    fdisk gdisk parted lvm2 \
    git openssh-client bash-completion \
    && apt-get clean && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*
CMD ["/bin/bash"]

#### Windows Notepad adds .txt. Save as Dockerfile, not Dockerfile.txt. Use ren Dockerfile.txt Dockerfile to fix.

Step 3: Create docker-compose.yml
Run notepad docker-compose.yml and paste:

version: '3.8'
services:
  my-ubuntu-lab:
    build: .
    image: full-ubuntu-lab:22.04
    container_name: my-ubuntu-lab
    hostname: ubuntu-lab
    privileged: true
    volumes:
      - /sys/fs/cgroup:/sys/fs/cgroup:ro
      - ubuntu_lab_home:/root
    tty: true
    stdin_open: true
    command: /bin/bash
volumes:
  ubuntu_lab_home:

Step 4: Build
docker compose up -d --build
You should see:

Image full-ubuntu-lab:22.04 Built
Network ubuntu-lab_default Created
Volume ubuntu_lab_home Created
Container my-ubuntu-lab Started

Step 5: Enter and Test
docker exec -it my-ubuntu-lab bash

Step 6: Daily Workflow
# Morning - Start
cd ~/ubuntu-lab
docker start my-ubuntu-lab
docker exec -it my-ubuntu-lab bash
# ... do Linux practice ...
# Exit & Stop
# Inside container:
exit
# Back in PowerShell:
docker stop my-ubuntu-lab